  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a medium the speed of light wave decreases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;times to its speed in free space. The ratio of relative permittivity to the refractive index of the medium is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ______.</p><p>(Given speed of light in free space <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and for the given medium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Speed of light in medium is related to speed of light in vacuum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and refractive index&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#956;</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Then, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Refractive index in terms of&nbsp;relative permeability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfenced></math>and relative permittivity<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfenced></math>&nbsp; of the medium is stated as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#956;</mi><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
